# JARDIM alone, a win in the 1995 controls: the three labyrinths and the final enemy, touched at
# 72250 (lives 2, 1500 points). The route is the closed-loop planner's (docs/jardim/DESIGN.md
# "Tests"): presses only (`hold KEY 1`, 30 ms apart: a 16-unit step or a 48-unit turn each),
# along the axes; it picks up a crossbow first, shoots the Bussuf and Alemao (and Siri with the
# bazooka) in a clear line ahead, walks around the others (not Chato: J2 keeps him), opens the
# doors on its way (SPACE), takes a medkit when health is low and takes the exit doors. The
# enemies animate and act on every frame, ten ticks a second (the frame cost).
# The second run has every bug fix on the 1995 controls (the Corrigida less its movement, keys,
# controls screen, J8 and the wall margin): the same game, the result differs by BUGS.md J1: the
# Original's "bonus" divides 10^9 by the low tick word less the start tick (+17870, won 19370),
# the fixed one by the milliseconds played (+13840, won 15340). The Corrigida's game is
# jardim-corrigida-alone-win.input.
#
#   zig-out/bin/noite --minigame jardim --headless --ms 75000 --input tools/play/jardim-alone-win.input
